      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Just as well, I've seen and been kicked by people purely just for their own entertainment, and people who just kick people because \"I don't know you\" or \"We're having a private discussion\" (Even though they intentionally opened it in a friends+ world). This system has been abused time and time again, and even I have done it unintentionally. When I first used the kick system, I thought it meant nothing to kick people, until I went out of my way to do the research, because people got really pissed with me (which is fair), and realized all the damage it causes. Some people don't even understand that kicking holds actual consequences, yet others enjoy abusing it just as much. I'm surprised I got Veteran. I got kicked quite often purely because someone didn't know me, or because they enjoyed kicking all of my friends and I simply because they could. \nI guess having a lot of content, friends, and hours under my belt adds up. As well as keeping to my own instances, trusted friends instances, or public worlds to avoid people abusing the kick feature. \n\nAll in all, I like the nuisance system, not the automated trust system. I really don't like the \"Report Abuse\" button either. I've used it at least 10 times throughout my time in VRChat, and not one admin has showed up. I just hope they think about the power they are giving to the user, as this system is most certainly a double edged sword.",
